{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I'll [C]twine 'mid the ringlets
Of my [G7]raven black [C]hair,
The [C]lilies so pale
And the [G7]roses so [C]fair,
The [C]myrtle so bright
With an [F]emerald [C]hue,
The [C]pale emanita
And [G7]eglantine [C]blue.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
He [C]told me he loved me,
And [G7]promised to [C]love,
Through [C]ill and misfortune,
All [G7]others a[C]bove;
A[C]nother has won him;
Ah, [F]misery to [C]tell;
He [C]left me in silence,
No [G7]word of fare[C]well!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
He [C]taught me to love him,
He [G7]called me his [C]flower
That [C]blossomed for him
All the [G7]brighter each [C]hour;
But I [C]woke from my dreaming,
My [F]idol was [C]clay;
My [C]visions of love
Have all [G7]faded a[C]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
I'll [C]think of him never!
I'll [G7]be wildly [C]gay;
I'll [C]charm every heart,
And the [G7]crowd I will [C]sway;
I'll [C]live yet to see him
Re[F]gret the dark [C]hour
When he [C]won, then neglected,
The [G7]frail wildwood [C]flower.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: C}
